# GEMINI_API_KEY: OPTIONAL. All AI features (chat, insights, receipt/inventory photo
# scanning) run server-side in the zad-core-intelligence Supabase Edge Function, on the
# Gemini key pool (ZAD_API_KEY_1..5) held in Supabase project secrets, NOT here.
# (This used to name zad-ai-proxy and GROQ_API_KEY; that function was deleted and the
# provider moved to Gemini — corrected 2026-09-05.)
# This key only powers an optional, dormant client path (ZadAiGeminiClient) that
# activates if a user manually pastes their own Gemini key into the app's camera
# screen. Leave the placeholder below if you don't have one; nothing breaks.
GEMINI_API_KEY=MY_GEMINI_API_KEY
# SUPABASE_URL: Your Supabase project URL (required)
SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
# SUPABASE_ANON_KEY: Your Supabase anonymous public key (required)
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key
# AMAZON_ASSOCIATE_TAG: Amazon Associates store ID used to build affiliate links
# (AffiliateHelper.kt) client-side. The amazon-creators-search Supabase Edge Function
# uses the same tag server-side via its own AMAZON_ASSOCIATE_TAG project secret.
AMAZON_ASSOCIATE_TAG=zad0b-21
# PEXELS_API_KEY: OPTIONAL. Food/recipe photos (Zad Chef cards, the recipe detail
# screen). Leave the placeholder and images still work: PexelsRepo falls back to the
# `pexels_image` action on zad-core-intelligence, which holds its own PEXELS_API_KEY as a
# Supabase project secret. Setting a real key here compiles it into the APK and lets the
# phone call Pexels directly (one less hop), at the cost of anyone who unpacks the APK
# being able to spend your free quota — which is why LOCATIONIQ_API_KEY is deliberately
# server-only. Same free key, so rotate it at pexels.com if it leaks; nothing else breaks.
PEXELS_API_KEY=MY_PEXELS_API_KEY
